Message-ID: <465dabf35323addc51630cdb15c24799978359fa.1792218164.git.claude@p7x.dev>
From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] mail: Thread each revision under its first version
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: okvpxwoktnozrkkqnvsyuutxsuzpwkok
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:23:02 +0000

Series posted before revisions replied to their first version are
each a chain of top-level threads, one per version, joined only by
the "Link to v(N-1)" line in each cover. Their history and review
are scattered across those threads, so following a series means
chasing links by hand.

Rewriting In-Reply-To and References on the older revisions makes the
existing list read the same way as series posted from now on, with
every version and its review in one thread. Only those two headers
change, in 123 messages; bodies and other headers are untouched.
---
change-id: okvpxwoktnozrkkqnvsyuutxsuzpwkok

base-branch: mail@upstream

This commit is already on mail@upstream as 465dabf35323, merged from
my claude bookmark together with the reply that announced it. This
mail puts it on the list for review and the record. Applying it again
to mail@upstream changes nothing.

It was made with "[PATCH v2] libexec/mail: Add rethread.py" in
~/lab/mail.jj:

    libexec/mail/rethread.py --apply maildir/cur

Checks done before committing:

- In each of the 123 files, every changed line is an In-Reply-To or
  References header, compared with the parent commit.
- A second dry run plans nothing.
- A notmuch database rebuilt from scratch has 103 threads, down from
  122, and each series is one tree.

To check it yourself, the diffstat below lists every file, and this
prints any changed line that is not one of the two headers (it
should print nothing):

    jj diff --git -r 465dabf35323 | grep '^[-+][^-+]' |
        grep -v '^[-+]\(In-Reply-To\|References\):' |
        grep -v '^[-+][[:space:]]'

notmuch new skips files whose names did not change, so rebuild the
database once to see the new threads:

    notmuch dump > /tmp/notmuch.tags
    mv <database path>/xapian <database path>/xapian.old
    notmuch new
    notmuch restore < /tmp/notmuch.tags

